b/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186201227}] :question/id #uuid "27de1ba1-abf8-5305-9395-914e41d9e20b" :question/math-academy-id "q-226130" :question/problem "The HR head of a large company wants to conduct a survey to estimate the difference in the proportion of employees from two departments who work overtime at least once a month. The summary statistics for samples from each department are given in the table below, where $n$ is the sample size and $p_{i}$ is the proportion of employees in Department $i$ who work overtime at least once a month.\n\n|  | Department 1 | Department 2 |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $n$ | $32$ | $50$ |\n| $p^(^)$ | $0.625$ | $0.7$ |\n\nFind a $99 \\mathrm{\\% }$ confidence interval for the difference $p_{1} - p_{2}$ between the corresponding population proportions.\n\n*Hint: Given a random variable $Z∼N(0, 1)$, the table below shows the $z$-scores $z_{p}$ such that $P(Z > z_{p}) = p$ for some particular values of $p$.*\n\n| $p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $z_{p}$ | $1.282$ | $1.645$ | $1.960$ | $2.326$ | $2.576$ |\n\nThe required confidence interval is\n$($\n{{field-1}}\n$$,\n{{field-2}}\n$)$.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204437 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203989 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4bf249b6-c944-5064-8e53-f1bd34bb5975" :knowledge-point/title "Finding MM Estimators for Bernoulli Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "e14c3dec-935a-5d3d-84e4-0eac1e39ae6c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186202582}] :question/id #uuid "cc068cf7-ea78-50c9-a9b7-050648061883" :question/math-academy-id "q-251302" :question/problem "Suppose $X_{1}, X_{2}, …, X_{8}$ is an I.I.D