ss $k^(^)$ as \"the value of $k$ that makes $p(k)$ as large as possible.\"\n\nWhich of the following correctly defines $k^(^)$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235520 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100893 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "99112850-043d-53e5-8d61-fecb0317bd11" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Particular Solutions of Differential Equations by Separating the Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b45fa11b-7aeb-5dbf-a888-002c910fdf5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25+3{e}^{-0.03t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234823}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b45fa11b-7aeb-5dbf-a888-002c910fdf5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25+3{e}^{-0.03t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234823} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba2c9880-594d-5761-a31f-7e56aaee7f89" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235200}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cdb03268-a0ae-53d3-84de-7af60bc110d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-168078" :question/problem "Let $\\overset{^}{T}(t)$ be a particular solution of the differential equation from the previous part that satisfies the condition $\\overset{^}{T}(0)=28.$ Find $\\overset{^}{T}(t).$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\overset{^}{T}(t)\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Previously, we found that the general solution is\n\n$$\nT=25+K{e}^{-0.03t}.\n$$\n\nwhere $K$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now apply the condition $T(0)=28$ to find $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}28 & =25+K\\,{e}^{-0.03(0)} \\\\ 28 & =25+K\\,{e}^{0} \\\\ K & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the required particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\overset{^}{T}(t)=25+3{e}^{-0.03t}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235521 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115372 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6835b52b-adaa-5c66-9f6d-d32591864659" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Infinite Limits Using the Laws of Exponents and the Algebra of Limits"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de450015-5aa8-5191-9a29-436c61bfb307" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234895}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de450015-5aa8-5191-9a29-436c61bfb307" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234895} :answer-field/id #uuid "9372c366-3893-5a0e-9fbb-ef1b020dbe47" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235151}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "90598903-81c5-5bc8-96e0-ec1e765e45c2" :question/math-academy-id "q-168079" :question/problem "For the function $\\overset{^}{T}(t)$ from the previous part, what is ${lim}_{t\\to \\,-\\infty }\\overset{^}{T}(t)?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${lim}_{t\\to \\,-\\infty }\\overset{^}{T}(t)\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "From the previous part, we know that\n\n$$\n\\overset{^}{T}(t)=25+3{e}^{-0.03t}.\n$$\n\nWe can use the laws of exponents and the algebra of limits to rewrite the given limit, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to \\,-\\infty }\\overset{^}{T}(t) & ={lim}_{t\\to \\,-\\infty }(25+3{e}^{-0.03t}) \\\\  & =25+3{lim}_{t\\to \\,-\\infty }{e}^{-0.03t} \\\\  & =25+3\\,{e}^{\\,\\,{lim}_{t\\to \\,-\\infty }(-0.03t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${e}^{\\,\\,{lim}_{t\\to \\,-\\infty }(-0.03t)}=\\infty ,$ and the positive factor of $3$ does not affect the sign of the limit, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{t\\to -\\,\\infty }\\overset{^}{T}(t)=\\infty .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412752 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157355 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b60ce582-4127-57b8-bba8-04cf17169ca3" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Population Mean From the Sample Mean"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bad6d10-02bb-565e-9e3d-fc4d56f3515f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412694} {:answer/id #uuid "19bf6f9a-c70f-54f2-bdbc-d7de758d6b9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412699} {:answer/id #uuid "55e0499b-82a7-5555-ad32-f3b98d2d802e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412712} {:answer/id #uuid "c5f2e157-ae58-57fd-a20d-e97626efe5ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412733} {:answer/id #uuid "f4a893b2-8685-577c-97ad-382d5e7f4531" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412741}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5f2e157-ae58-57fd-a20d-e97626efe5ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412733} :answer-field/id #uuid "82968c5a-55cf-5036-a4f7-86e133d5bca1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412746}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1efe5ada-0d49-54bc-8531-cf777586f9d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-149732" :question/problem "Suppose the following data is sampled from a population. Compute an estimate for the population mean.\n\n$$\n-8,\\,5,\\,-14,\\,-20,\\,16\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sequence of random variables representing a random sample of size $n$ drawn from a population with the population mean $\\mu .$ \nThen, the sample mean $\\overset{―}{X}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{X}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{X}_{i}.\n$$\n\nNote that:\n\n- $\\overset{―}{X}$ is the mean value of ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n},$ while $\\overset{¯}{x}$ is the mean of a specific sample ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$\n\n- the sample mean $\\overset{―}{X}$ is an estimator of the population mean $\\mu ,$ and\n\n- the value $\\overset{^}{\\mu }=\\overset{¯}{x}$ is an estimate of the population mean $\\mu .$\n\nTherefore, our estimate for the population mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{\\mu } & =\\overset{―}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(-8+5-14-20+16) \\\\  & =-\\frac{21}{5} \\\\  & =-4.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412754 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157355 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b60ce582-4127-57b8-bba8-04cf17169ca3" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Population Mean From the Sample Mean"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c9718c7-902f-5345-ad03-482984e9c1fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412695} {:answer/id #uuid "1dd3b9ac-3e11-5981-a4d8-309f740a2b9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412700} {:answer/id #uuid "5fbe3e02-0a60-5155-aaa9-1099c2486ac5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412713} {:answer/id #uuid "635832eb-ba37-5e03-b2a0-da170625a38a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412715} {:answer/id #uuid "ea847776-7f1b-5b89-bb47-fd8b7fc0ef23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412739}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1dd3b9ac-3e11-5981-a4d8-309f740a2b9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412700} :answer-field/id #uuid "05770093-228f-5a71-80b2-0c344bf688cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412742}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8d4c868b-7564-5dcc-a2d7-26fd40beb90e" :question/math-academy-id "q-88951" :question/problem "Suppose the following data is sampled from a population. Compute an estimate for the population mean.\n\n$$\n4,\\,-7,\\,6,\\,-3,\\,5,\\,-2\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sequence of random variables representing a random sample of size $n$ drawn from a population with the population mean $\\mu .$ \nThen, the sample mean $\\overset{―}{X}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{X}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{X}_{i}.\n$$\n\nNote that:\n\n- $\\overset{―}{X}$ is the mean value of ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n},$ while $\\overset{¯}{x}$ is the mean of a specific sample ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$\n\n- the sample mean $\\overset{―}{X}$ is an estimator of the population mean $\\mu ,$ and\n\n- the value $\\overset{^}{\\mu }=\\overset{¯}{x}$ is an estimate of the population mean $\\mu .$\n\nTherefore, our estimate for the population mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{\\mu } & =\\overset{―}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{6}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(4-7+6-3+5-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{6} \\\\  & =0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412755 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157355 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b60ce582-4127-57b8-bba8-04cf17169ca3" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Population Mean From the Sample Mean"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "153032cc-4283-545e-a6a0-cefb36c3114d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412698} {:answer/id #uuid "2153f32d-f2c3-577b-ae14-a4cecc082caf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19.0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412703} {:answer/id #uuid "44ce75c3-7e0f-5153-960b-ad3e37103a25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412709} {:answer/id #