& =\\frac{121}{5} \\\\  & =24.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412757 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157355 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b60ce582-4127-57b8-bba8-04cf17169ca3" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Population Mean From the Sample Mean"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05b86b9d-3da6-5793-a9a2-ff8597d2d88f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412692} {:answer/id #uuid "64662eb3-5019-553c-8275-382223e2cb35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412716} {:answer/id #uuid "bee938dd-06c2-5f9c-8ef9-0f8d393a8280" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10.75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412729} {:answer/id #uuid "e28998a7-4d68-5d5a-a55b-33ee2914774d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412737} {:answer/id #uuid "e37df5d9-6f3f-5219-8dd9-a68efc7b5e0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412738}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e28998a7-4d68-5d5a-a55b-33ee2914774d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412737} :answer-field/id #uuid "967125f4-f40d-593b-92b5-aa4cbabd7b80" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412748}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "da6b0f51-7da3-5f92-8b12-f21abc3a1502" :question/math-academy-id "q-149729" :question/problem "Suppose the following data is sampled from a population. Compute an estimate for the population mean.\n\n$$\n13,\\,12,\\,9,\\,3\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sequence of random variables representing a random sample of size $n$ drawn from a population with the population mean $\\mu .$ \nThen, the sample mean $\\overset{―}{X}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{X}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{X}_{i}.\n$$\n\nNote that:\n\n- $\\overset{―}{X}$ is the mean value of ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n},$ while $\\overset{¯}{x}$ is the mean of a specific sample ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$\n\n- the sample mean $\\overset{―}{X}$ is an estimator of the population mean $\\mu ,$ and\n\n- the value $\\overset{^}{\\mu }=\\overset{¯}{x}$ is an estimate of the population mean $\\mu .$\n\nTherefore, our estimate for the population mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{\\mu } & =\\overset{―}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(13+12+9+3) \\\\  & =\\frac{37}{4} \\\\  & =9.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412760 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157355 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b60ce582-4127-57b8-bba8-04cf17169ca3" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Population Mean From the Sample Mean"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a8f0bd0-23b0-55c2-ac0d-7b2cdb3481d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412693} {:answer/id #uuid "143d8ae2-eeb0-5785-9404-9aa0bd8db8b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412697} {:answer/id #uuid "1dfb0748-171c-5468-bfd1-1bcd7e123168" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412701} {:answer/id #uuid "24294c8f-833d-5c05-bbe8-7de4894ddace" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412705} {:answer/id #uuid "aeae6d43-d40a-56db-bc