ligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{4}(19-14+22-21) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{4} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The mean of the squared data is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{4}({19}^{2}+(-14)^{2}+{22}^{2}+(-21)^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\,482}{4} \\\\  & =370.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-{(\\overset{―}{x})}^{2} & =370.5-{1.5}^{2} \\\\  & =368.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the sample variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\overset{^}{\\sigma }}^{2} & ={s}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{n}{n-1}[\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-{(\\overset{―}{x})}^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{4-1}\\cdot 368.25 \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\,473}{3} \\\\  & =491.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, an unbiased estimate of the population variance is $491.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443486 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184194 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "897ae010-a9a2-5971-a1ec-c2618cb8ad2c" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Population Variance From Sample Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3009f909-e476-50ba-a047-197b6a85673b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "62.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443420} {:answer/id #uuid "63de4533-90d1-5673-94b5-dca8efe8b5f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "71.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443431} {:answer/id #uuid "c5252f71-8ab7-57cf-b784-74a395cd1b58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443447} {:answer/id #uuid "e38e698d-13ff-5433-b5e1-e34e1dad7c6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "70" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443457} {:answer/id #uuid "ff54205f-411e-56f3-aefd-b6d54fdc08ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "77.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443466}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff54205f-411e-56f3-aefd-b6d54fdc08ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "77.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443466} :answer-field/id #uuid "86777429-62e1-5a84-a748-657f0d5246f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443471}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9d145845-d1fd-557d-b5dc-7262bedf9b90" :question/math-academy-id "q-89001" :question/problem "Suppose the following data is sampled from a population. Compute an unbiased estimate of the population variance.\n\n$$\n-6,\\,7,\\,10,\\,-9,\\,8\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…{X}_{n}$ is a sequence of random variables representing a random sample of size $n$ drawn from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population variance ${\\sigma }^{2}.$ Then, the sample variance ${S}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{S}^{2}=\\frac{1}{n-1}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{({X}_{i}-\\overset{―}{X})}^{2}=\\frac{n}{n-1}[\\overset{―}{{X}^{2}}-{(\\overset{―}{X})}^{2}].\n$$\n\nNote that:\n\n- $\\overset{―}{X}$ is the sample mean,\n\n- the sample variance ${S}^{2}$ is an unbiased estimator of the population variance ${\\sigma }^{2},$ and\n\n- ${\\overset{^}{\\sigma }}^{2}={s}^{2}$ denotes the unbiased estimate of ${\\sigma }^{2}$ computed from the sample ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}.$\n\nFirst, we will compute the quantity\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-{(\\overset{―}{x})}^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe proceed as follows:\n\n- The mean of the data is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{5}(-6+7+10-9+8) \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{5} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The mean of the squared data is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{5}[(-6)^{2}+{7}^{2}+{10}^{2}+(-9)^{2}+{8}^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{330}{5} \\\\  & =66.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-{(\\overset{―}{x})}^{2} & =66-{2}^{2} \\\\  & =62.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the sample variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\overset{^}{\\sigma }}^{2} & ={s}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{n}{n-1}[\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-{(\\overset{―}{x})}^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{5-1}\\cdot 62 \\\\  & =\\frac{310}{4} \\\\  & =77.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, an unbiased estimate of the population variance is $77.5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443487 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184208 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2aa1599e-b9c0-5282-ac58-b10211cb7d30" :knowledge-point/title "Computing an Estimate of the Population Variance"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d937d0f-642b-5b54-95f1-386570968e23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443416} {:answer/id #uuid "5f99ee14-f921-55bb-beae-94d55f4763f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443429} {:answer/id #uuid "7682beb4-209c-5c8e-b02c-5574fd9c52a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443436} {:answer/id #uuid "a8bb74fe-3173-5959-9647-a075edc932ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443441} {:answer/id #uuid "d6f4d205-ccff-5bbf-b86d-955d5121dea6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443455}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f99ee14-f921-55bb-beae-94d55f4763f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443429} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a76954e-73f1-5964-bd22-6c22516b62a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443470}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c0d91061-b2d9-57bd-a897-ea0b99d019a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-139847" :question/problem "A random sample of size $n=11$ is conducted from a population. It is known that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{11}{({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})}^{2}=220\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere each ${x}_{i}$ is a sample observation. Compute an unbiased estimate of the population variance." :question/worked-solution "Suppose ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…{X}_{n}$ is a sequence of random variables representing a random sample of size $n$ drawn from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population variance ${\\sigma }^{2}.$ Then, the sample variance ${S}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{S}^{2}=\\frac{1}{n-1}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{({X}_{i}-\\overset{―}{X})}^{2}=\\frac{n}{n-1}[\\overset{―}{{X}^{2}}-{(\\overset{―}{X})}^{2}].\n$$\n\nNote that:\n\n- $\\overset{―}{X}$ is the sample mean,\n\n- the sample variance ${S}^{2}$ is an unbiased estimator of the population variance ${\\sigma }^{2},$ and\n\n- ${\\overset{^}{\\sigma }}^{2}={s}^{2}$ denotes an unbiased estimate of ${\\sigma }^{2}$ that's computed from the sample ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}.$\n\nWe're given that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{11}{({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})}^{2}=220$ and $n=11.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\overset{^}{\\sigma }}^{2} & ={s}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{n-1}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{11-1}\\cdot 220 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\cdot 220 \\\\  & =22.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, an unbiased estimate of the population variance is $22.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443488 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184194 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "897ae010-a9a2-5971-a1ec-c2618cb8ad2c" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Population Variance From Sample Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15c9d