max}_{y\\in \\{3,7,11,15\\}}g(y).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543550 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176033 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e77a14c-9943-5494-ae89-a77c7a1888d0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Residuals From a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "111c354b-41eb-5072-82a1-a27b376ef779" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15\\,kg" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542679} {:answer/id #uuid "32b8dd5f-70e9-5121-9de5-389361fe1956" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-25\\,kg" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542777} {:answer/id #uuid "3eb6331c-9c5e-5112-8172-2d2c6ae715e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20\\,kg" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542810} {:answer/id #uuid "5ecc3dc4-f5bd-51df-a791-7eef362a46eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50\\,kg" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542895} {:answer/id #uuid "6748c281-3aeb-5426-9750-d7329ae49821" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15\\,kg" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542918}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32b8dd5f-70e9-5121-9de5-389361fe1956" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-25\\,kg" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542777} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ed40114-2ba1-5996-b505-11a621544fa9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543401}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b2848e9c-e485-5752-8daf-a5d57b496ccb" :question/math-academy-id "q-134812" :question/problem "![](images/24/243a4212d1128a79203493bf672ad1c956fe0f48aad6abbb910de2861d99669c.png)\n\nA dog food company records data on the number of dogs $(x)$ sheltered at some kennels across the country and the corresponding amount of dog food $y$ (in kilograms) consumed in a month. The scatter plot for the data and the corresponding linear regression line are shown above. \n\nAccording to the regression model, what is the residual for the highlighted data point?" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(10,175).$ So, our actual value is $y=175.$\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=10$ has the $y$-coordinate $200.$ So, our estimated value is $\\overset{^}{y}=200.$\n\n![](images/2c/2cd59a9ae9c7ad474a9d5a308d4b8f3c9b96be70acdf1e3613dfc4757ff01766.png)\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =175-200 \\\\  & =-25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is $-25\\,kg.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543562 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176033 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e77a14c-9943-5494-ae89-a77c7a1888d0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Residuals From a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00765988-b24e-516e-81a5-803465b2cbab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542636} {:answer/id #uuid "2fb61cf0-8148-5e19-85df-5a17cfbc10f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542766} {:answer/id #uuid "6dfd5478-a857-5295-91e8-3b663a1bc7a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542933} {:answer/id #uuid "ba0a7473-8f7d-5f9a-97c9-726d94e6f4b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543126} {:answer/id #uuid "f0b10261-e8cd-557e-a60d-49043c55ee7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543256}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba0a7473-8f7d-5f9a-97c9-726d94e6f4b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543126} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8c336d7-1f88-5669-a3cc-3ac8dd456feb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543428}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d6509173-6968-54cb-999d-d5fe096ebbff" :question/math-academy-id "q-134798" :question/problem "![](images/b3/b375c1e162a9f1c2892903c20606921673498579f9b41f633447832fd3ea2192.png)\n\nThe scatter plot for the data sets $x$ and $y$ of paired observations and the corresponding linear regression line are shown above.\n\nAccording to the regression model, what is the residual for the highlighted datapoint?" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(4,70).$ So, our actual value is $y=70.$\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=4$ has the $y$-coordinate $50.$ So, our estimated value of is $\\overset{^}{y}=50.$\n\n![](images/04/041f64255345edf7ac37bd61e0ab97a93cc2696f028a53ba0896e0659966c2d8.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, the residual is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =70-50 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] 